STEP 1 — PARSE XML
==================

XmlPath xp = new XmlPath(rs.asString());

XmlPath parses the XML response so that we can read
and extract data from its structure.

Note:
asString() / asPrettyString() → Response Body as String
asPrettyString() → mainly for readable display
asString() → commonly used for parsing


STEP 2 — CHECK DATA IS PRESENT
==============================

String container = xp.getList("breakfast_menu").toString();

Assert.assertTrue(container.contains("Strawberry"));

Flow:

XML → XmlPath → getList() → List → toString() → String → contains()


STEP 3 — VALIDATE PARTICULAR VALUE
===================================

Example:

French Toast → $4.50

Step A: Get Names and Prices

List<String> names =
        xp.getList("breakfast_menu.food.name");

List<String> prices =
        xp.getList("breakfast_menu.food.price");


Step B: Find French Toast position

int indexOfFrench = names.indexOf("French Toast");


Step C: Get price using the same position

String priceOfFrench = prices.get(indexOfFrench);


Step D: Assert

Assert.assertEquals(priceOfFrench, "$4.50");


IMPORTANT CONCEPT:

names.indexOf("French Toast")
        ↓
       3

prices.get(3)
        ↓
     "$4.50"

So we use the position/index from the NAME list
to find the corresponding value from the PRICE list.